.\" Manual page for telegram-send-py.
.\" View locally with: man ./extras/telegram-send.1
.TH TELEGRAM-SEND 1 "2026-10-15" "telegram-send-py 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
telegram-send, telegram-listen, telegram-integration \- send and receive Telegram messages
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B telegram-send
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIMESSAGE\fR
.br
.B telegram-listen
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.br
.B telegram-integration
\fICOMMAND\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B telegram-send-py
is a small command\-line front end for the Telegram Bot API. It can send a
single message to a chat or channel, and listen for incoming updates while
optionally triggering external scripts for every received message.
.PP
Three entry points are installed. The
.B telegram-send
and
.B telegram-listen
commands each wrap a single action, while
.B telegram-integration
exposes both as subcommands together with shell completion generation.
.SH COMMANDS
The unified
.B telegram-integration
command exposes the following subcommands:
.TP
.B send
Send a single message. Accepts the same options as
.BR telegram-send .
.TP
.B listen
Continuously poll for new updates until interrupted (Ctrl+C). Accepts the same
options as
.BR telegram-listen .
.TP
.B completion
Print a shell completion script to standard output. Takes the shell name
(\fBbash\fR, \fBzsh\fR or \fBfish\fR) as its argument; use
.B \-\-program
to generate the script for a different command name.
.SH OPTIONS
Options shared by the sending and listening commands:
.TP
.BR \-\-token " " \fITOKEN\fR
Telegram bot token. Overrides the value in the configuration file and the
.B TELEGRAM_TOKEN
environment variable.
.TP
.BR \-\-channel\-id " " \fICHAT\fR
Target channel or chat. Overrides the value in the configuration file and the
.B TELEGRAM_CHANNEL_ID
environment variable.
.SS Send options
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-mode " " \fIMODE\fR
Message parse mode: \fBmarkdown\fR (default), \fBhtml\fR or \fBplain\fR.
.SS Listen options
.TP
.BR \-\-timeout " " \fISECONDS\fR
Long\-polling timeout in seconds (default: 30).
.TP
.BR \-\-interval " " \fISECONDS\fR
Delay between polls in seconds (default: 1.0).
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-scripts " " \fIPATH\fR
External script to run for every received message. May be given multiple
times. The full update is exported as JSON through the
.B TELEGRAM_MESSAGE
environment variable.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Credentials are read from
.I ~/.config/telegram-send/config.toml
(or
.IB $XDG_CONFIG_HOME /telegram-send/config.toml
when set) using a small TOML file:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
token   = "123456:ABC\-DEF"
chat_id = "@your_channel"
.fi
.RE
.PP
Keep the file private, for example with \fBchmod 600\fR.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TELEGRAM_TOKEN
Fallback bot token used when the configuration file is absent.
.TP
.B TELEGRAM_CHANNEL_ID
Fallback channel or chat id used when the configuration file is absent.
.TP
.B TELEGRAM_MESSAGE
Set by
.B telegram-listen
for every triggered script; contains the JSON\-encoded Telegram update.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/telegram-send/config.toml
User configuration (bot token and chat id).
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/telegram-send/state.db
SQLite database storing the last processed update offset.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B telegram-send "**Hello** from *Telegram*"
Send a Markdown message.
.TP
.B telegram-send "<b>Hello</b>" \-m html
Send an HTML message.
.TP
.B telegram-listen \-\-scripts ./handler.py
Listen and run a script for every incoming message.
.TP
.B telegram-integration completion bash > /etc/bash_completion.d/telegram-integration
Generate a Bash completion script.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR systemd.service (5)
.PP
Project page: <https://github.com/vmgabriel/telegram-send-py>
.SH AUTHOR
Gabriel Vargas Monroy.
